":false,"topics":["canvas","chart","graph","html5","html5-charts","javascript"],"visibility":"public","forks":11988,"open_issues":505,"watchers":66876,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/pulls/7883","html_url":"https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/pull/7883","diff_url":"https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/pull/7883.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/pull/7883.patch","merged_at":"2020-10-17T20:35:01Z"},"body":"Calling Math.max with a large number of values was throwing an exception.\r\nTracking the current largest width and height as the widths and heights are\r\nbuilt up should be faster and avoids the exception.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease consider the following before submitting a pull request:\r\n\r\nGuidelines for contributing: https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/blob/master/docs/docs/developers/contributing.md\r\n\r\nExample of changes on an interactive website such as the following:\r\n- https://jsbin.com/\r\n- https://jsfiddle.net/\r\n- https://codepen.io/pen/\r\n- Premade template: https://codepen.io/pen?template=JXVYzq\r\n-->\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/7883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/7883/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/comments/708105164","html_url":"https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/7881#issuecomment-708105164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/7881","id":708105164,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcwODEwNTE2NA==","user":{"login":"davidspencerward","id":53668425,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjY4NDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53668425?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward","html_url":"https://github.com/davidspencerward","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-10-14T01:52:12Z","updated_at":"2020-10-14T01:52:12Z","body":"Evert:\r\n\r\nAwesome. That works and improves everything!!!! Zooming is 1,000 times faster now.\r\n\r\nThanks for the quick response!!!\r\n\r\nDavid\r\n\r\n\r\n[https://www.cisco.com/c/dam/m/en_us/signaturetool/images/banners/standard/03_standard_indigoblue.png]\r\nDavid Ward\r\nTECHNICAL LEADER.SOFTWARE ENGINEERING-DEVELOPMENT\r\ndaviwar2@cisco.com<mailto:daviwar2@cisco.com>\r\nTel:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCisco Systems, Inc.\r\n8135 Maple Lawn Blvd.\r\nFULTON\r\n20759\r\nUnited States\r\ncisco.com\r\n[http://www.cisco.com/assets/swa/img/thinkbeforeyouprint.gif]\r\nThink before you print.\r\nThis email may contain confidential and privileged material for the sole use of the intended recipient. Any review, use, distribution or disclosure by others is strictly prohibited. If you are not the intended recipient (or authorized to receive for the recipient), please contact the sender by reply email and delete all copies of this message.\r\nPlease click here<http://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/legal/terms-sale-software-license-agreement/company-registration-information.html> for Company Registration Information.\r\n\r\n\r\nFrom: Evert Timberg <notifications@github.com>\r\nSent: Tuesday, October 13, 2020 6:12 PM\r\nTo: chartjs/Chart.js <Chart.js@noreply.github.com>\r\nCc: David Ward (daviwar2) <daviwar2@cisco.com>; Mention <mention@noreply.github.com>\r\nSubject: Re: [chartjs/Chart.js] Using version 2.9.3 gets Maximum call stack size exceeded exception in google chrome. (#7881)\r\n\r\n\r\nThe issue seems to be related to stepSize: 1. If I remove that, it's not a problem. I'm guessing that when stepSize is 1, there are too many ticks and we run out of memory when measuring the text.\r\n\r\n—\r\nYou are receiving this because you were mentioned.\r\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/7881#issuecomment-708037337>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AMZOUSMTNOO5TJEWLHXZC7LSKTGC5ANCNFSM4SPRXBWQ>.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chartjs/Chart.js/issues/comments/708105164/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"davidspencerward","id":53668425,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjY4NDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53668425?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward","html_url":"https://github.com/davidspencerward","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspencerward/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidspenc